  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards gender transformative education systems in Eastern Africa.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Many learners in Eastern Africa, has still deprived of both their right and access to education and COVID-19 crisis has exacerbated existing vulnerabilities and educational inequalities, impacting particularly girl&apos;s that are already at risk to gender-based violence, including unintended pregnancy. The priority to ensure continuity learning did not address the increased existing gender gaps related to enrolment, retention and ICT skills that was although some policies were put in place. To respond to those issues, UNESCO will support countries in the region to implement gender transformative education notably through STEM; Higher Education; Skills-based Education; Advocacy and ICT &amp; Digital Skills for girls and women.</narrative>
  </description>
